From 8ec54d0a519a7d5f5074f52e1649bea78b33db39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:48:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A session's cold first read sends only the turns its line
 estimate needs to cover the viewport, while an older page read on scroll-up
 still covers two more screens, so opening a session reads and builds rows for
 the fewest whole turns that fill its first screen (two of twenty on the
 benchmark's 1 MiB size-latency session and one of eighty on the 8 MiB one at
 a 32-row viewport) and the first scroll-up starts the older page read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QtZVtcNTgBwKhSN8i2v1w2
